+# Why the USDC balance vanished (and how to fix it for real)
+
+Short version: `useScaffoldReadContract` can only read contracts that Scaffold-ETH
+knows about by name. `"USDC"` was never registered in the right file, so the hook
+had no address/ABI to call, silently did nothing, and returned `undefined`. The
+teammate registered it in the wrong file — one that `yarn deploy` regenerates from
+scratch — so the fix got erased. The correct home is `externalContracts.ts`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why the hook returned `undefined` silently instead of erroring
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` doesn't take an address. It takes a **name** and resolves
+it internally:
+
+```
+useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC", ... })
+        │
+        ├─ useDeployedContractInfo("USDC")   // name → { address, abi }
+        │        └─ looks up contracts[targetChainId]["USDC"]
+        │           in the MERGED map of deployedContracts + externalContracts
+        │
+        └─ useReadContract({ address, abi, functionName, args, query: { enabled } })
+                                  ▲       ▲
+                          undefined   undefined   ← name wasn't found
+```
+
+Two design choices combine to make the failure silent:
+
+1. **Missing name → `undefined`, not a throw.** `useDeployedContractInfo` just does a
+   dictionary lookup by name on the current chain. A miss returns
+   `deployedContractData: undefined`. It does not raise.
+
+2. **wagmi disables the query when there's no address/ABI.** With `address` and `abi`
+   both `undefined`, the underlying `useReadContract` is effectively disabled (Scaffold
+   also gates `query.enabled`). A disabled query never fires — so:
+   - no network request (nothing in the Network tab — correct, it never happened),
+   - no runtime error (there was nothing to fail),
+   - `data` stays `undefined`, and `usdcBalance` renders as nothing.
+
+So "no error, no request, no data" is exactly the signature of an **unregistered
+contract name**, not of a failed call. The one place it *does* complain is the
+TypeScript compiler: `contractName` is a union of the known contract names, so
+`"USDC"` is a type error. But `next dev` renders anyway (type errors print in the
+terminal, they don't block the dev server), which is why nothing surfaced in the app.
+
+> Debugging tip for next time: an unregistered name is silent in the browser but loud
+> in the dev-server terminal (TS union error on `contractName`). Check there first.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Why the teammate's fix self-destructed on `yarn deploy`
+
+They pasted the USDC entry into:
+
+```
+packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+```
+
+That file is **auto-generated**. Its header literally says so:
+
+```ts
+/**
+ * This file is autogenerated by Scaffold-ETH.
+ * You should not edit it manually or your changes might be overwritten.
+ */
+```
+
+`yarn deploy` runs the Hardhat deploy scripts and then regenerates
+`deployedContracts.ts` **from scratch** out of the deployment artifacts in
+`packages/hardhat/deployments/` (via the `generateTsAbis` step). USDC is not one of
+*your* deployments — there's no artifact for it — so the regenerator rebuilt the file
+without it. The manual entry was overwritten and disappeared.
+
+It "worked all week" only because nobody redeployed all week. The manual edit was
+living in a file whose entire contents are disposable output. The first `yarn deploy`
+reset it.
+
+---
+
+## 3. The correct registration
+
+USDC is an **external / pre-existing** contract (Circle deployed it, you didn't), so it
+belongs in the hand-maintained file that the deploy pipeline never touches:
+
+```
+packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+```
+
+Scaffold merges `externalContracts` with `deployedContracts` before name lookup, so
+once USDC lives here, `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` resolves
+forever — and survives every `yarn deploy`. It also fixes the TypeScript union, so
+`"USDC"` becomes a valid `contractName`.
+
+Key it by **chain id 8453 (Base mainnet)** and use the **native Circle USDC** address
+(6 decimals):
+
+`0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`
+
+```ts
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+import { GenericContractsDeclaration } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth/contract";
+
+/**
+ * Contracts you did NOT deploy (tokens, protocols, etc.).
+ * Hand-maintained — yarn deploy never overwrites this file.
+ */
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "balanceOf",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [{ name: "account", type: "address" }],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "decimals",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint8" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "symbol",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "string" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "transfer",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "to", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "approve",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "allowance",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "owner", type: "address" },
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+No change to the `/payouts` page is needed — the existing hook call now resolves.
+
+### Notes
+- **Include only the ABI fragments you use** (above is a practical ERC-20 subset).
+  `balanceOf` alone is enough for the payouts read, but `decimals`/`transfer`/`approve`
+  are handy for formatting and payouts.
+- **6 decimals**, not 18 — format with `formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)`.
+- **Chain id must match your target network.** The key `8453` is Base mainnet. If you
+  test against a fork or another chain, add that chain id too, or the lookup misses on
+  that network (same silent-`undefined` behavior).
+- Don't confuse native USDC with bridged **USDbC**
+  (`0xd9aAEc86B65D86f6A7B5B1b0c42FFA531710b6CA`) — different token, different balance.
+```

